Remaining production gaps
These are not current test failures, but should be addressed before a public launch:

No /api/health health-check endpoint.
Database schema changes still use manual ALTER TABLE; proper migrations are needed.
SQLite is not ideal for multi-worker production.
Redis must be provisioned and tested in the deployment environment.
Google OAuth has not been tested with real Google credentials.
External threat APIs need live production testing and monitoring.
ML dataset is small and model quality is limited; current F1 is approximately 0.57.
No automated browser/UI integration tests.
Admin features are not implemented.
Production logging, backups, monitoring, and rollback procedures are still missing.
There is also one expected warning from Flask-Login about deprecated datetime.utcnow() inside the dependency.